// MedLevo Study Book (§24) and summaries (§31): sectioned artifacts generated by a resumable job (§53, AC-25).
//
//  * sections come from the processed structure: heading regions start a section; no headings → one section per
//    page; very long sections are split at page boundaries. Each section keeps its source region ids.
//  * one job per artifact version; every section is generated, validated and written in ONE transaction together
//    with its 'complete' status, then checkpointed. An interrupted section is regenerated from scratch on retry —
//    never published half-finished — and finished sections are never generated twice.
//  * the artifact is 'generating' while sections run (finished sections can be read, clearly labelled as a
//    draft in progress with real section counts); 'published' when every section is done, 'partial' when some
//    failed (listed), 'failed' when none succeeded.
//  * regeneration creates a NEW version of the lineage; the previous published version stays until the new one
//    is published (then 'superseded', unless frozen). block_keys derive from section + region ids, so notes keep
//    their semantic anchors; anchors whose block disappeared are listed as needs_reanchor — never moved (AC-22).
//  * summaries use the same machinery with page batches and honest coverage (never «complete» when pages are
//    unprocessed / unreadable / excluded; last-minute & high-yield are labelled as selections).
